         description = '''Find the syntax elements of C source code, for syntax highlighting.
                          Fredrik Öhrström (c) 2026 spdx: MIT

                          Unlike c.ixml this grammar parses the raw source, before the preprocessor, and
                          every character of the source is kept, so the text of the parse is the source.
                          Whitespace and punctuation are plain text, the rest is marked up:

                            comment    /* ... */ and // ...
                            preproc    a preprocessor line, with the directive as pp, eg #include,
                                       the included file as header and a defined name as macro
                            string     "..."            char       '...'
                            number     12, 0x1f, 1.5e3f
                            keyword    if, return, struct, typedef...
                            primitive  int, char, bool, size_t, uint32_t...
                            type       a name starting with an upper case letter that has a lower case
                                       letter, eg XMQDoc
                            macro      a name with only upper case letters, digits and _, eg NULL, XMQ_ATTRS
