         version     = 1a
         summary     = 'Render a TAF forecast, parsed with taf.ixml, as a web page:'
         description = 'Render a TAF forecast, parsed with taf.ixml, as a web page:
                          xmq ixml:meas/taf taf.inp xsl:meas/taf-to-html to-html > taf.html

                        A blue header shows the station, the issue time, the validity period, the
                        flight category (VFR, MVFR, IFR, LIFR) of the base forecast and the maximum
                        and minimum temperatures.

                        A timeline spans the validity period. The prevailing conditions, the base
                        forecast and the FM groups, are drawn on the first row, every BECMG, TEMPO,
                        INTER and PROB group gets a row of its own. The bars are colored by the
                        flight category of their conditions, a BECMG bar fades into the new
                        conditions that then last until the next FM group.

                        Below every period gets a card with a weather icon, the wind arrow, the
                        visibility, the weather and the cloud layers with their okta symbols.')
    file(path        = meas/taf-to-html_v1a.xslq
         size        = 71785
         sha256      = e12b812c54e25b1340c6e1f865b5e816a2cd62c0382038f57ff52de9f063385e
         mtime       = 2026-11-22T15:18:11Z
         version     = 1a
         summary     = 'Render a TAF forecast, parsed with taf.ixml, as a web page:'
         description = 'Render a TAF forecast, parsed with taf.ixml, as a web page:
                          xmq ixml:meas/taf taf.inp xsl:meas/taf-to-html to-html > taf.html

                        A blue header shows the station, the issue time, the validity period, the
                        flight category (VFR, MVFR, IFR, LIFR) of the base forecast and the maximum
                        and minimum temperatures.

                        A timeline spans the validity period. The prevailing conditions, the base
                        forecast and the FM groups, are drawn on the first row, every BECMG, TEMPO,
                        INTER and PROB group gets a row of its own. The bars are colored by the
                        flight category of their conditions, a BECMG bar fades into the new
                        conditions that then last until the next FM group.

                        Below every period gets a card with a weather icon, the wind arrow, the
                        visibility, the weather and the cloud layers with their okta symbols.')
    file(path        = meas/taf.ixml
         size        = 11588
         sha256      = 736cf47a900f7f7b8f34a8379610f91944c6379350b5ab9a06fd98c0b2164162
         mtime       = 2026-11-22T15:18:11Z
         version     = 1b
         summary     = 'A grammar for parsing TAF terminal aerodrome forecasts.'
         description = 'A grammar for parsing TAF terminal aerodrome forecasts.

                        Public Domain LLM-generated code (spdx: CC0)

                        The forecast is split into the base forecast, the conditions expected
                        for the whole validity period, followed by a change element for every
                        change group, FM (from), BECMG (becoming), TEMPO (temporarily),
                        INTER (intermittently) and PROB30/PROB40, that holds the conditions
                        it changes. The groups may be written on several lines.

                        Codes are kept, and a sibling -info element explains them in plain words.
                        Numbers are normalized like in metar.ixml: leading zeros are removed, M
                        becomes a minus sign and cloud bases are given in feet.

                        Example forecasts:
                        TAF EGLL 201059Z 2012/2118 24012KT 9999 SCT030 TEMPO 2012/2016 4000 SHRA BKN014
                            BECMG 2020/2023 VRB03KT PROB30 2103/2108 0800 FG BKN002
                        TAF AMD KJFK 201745Z 2018/2124 24015G25KT P6SM SCT050
                            FM202200 30010KT P6SM FEW250 TX25/2019Z TN14/2110Z

                        Not supported: the old validity periods with 6 digits (eg 051212), the
                        military icing and turbulence groups and the QNH groups.')
    file(path        = meas/taf_v1.ixml
         size        = 11588
         sha256      = 736cf47a900f7f7b8f34a8379610f91944c6379350b5ab9a06fd98c0b2164162
